# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies (repo-wide: sibling projects each have their own node_modules)
**/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
**/coverage

# next.js (repo-wide: multiple Next.js apps live in this monorepo)
**/.next/
**/out/

# production
**/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
!.env.local.example

# vercel
.vercel

# MCP server config references env vars, not secrets, but keep it local anyway
.mcp.json

# Claude Code local (machine-specific) state — every project folder has one
**/.claude/

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Generic per-language build artifacts, wherever they show up.
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/

# Sibling project folders: confirmed (2025-09-13) each is its own independent
# project with its own git repo and deploy target — not part of this site's
# codebase, so excluded wholesale rather than tracked here.
/Ai Automation Drone/
/IDS(Intrusion Detection system)/
/Wifi deauthentication/
/Inventory Management System/

.vercel
.env*
